  "reason": "Evidence: The best result so far is config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) at 0.591 acc, showing that multiprofile+avgpool is a strong configuration and PCA is a reasonable baseline encoder. Image alone is very weak (0.208), so multimodal gains are uncertain. Uncertainty: We don't yet know whether a learned RNA encoder (scvi_n200) can outperform PCA in the multiprofile+avgpool setting, which is the single most impactful design axis remaining for the RNA modality. This experiment (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) isolates the RNA encoder effect while holding the best profile and aggregation fixed, giving a clean comparison against config_002. If scvi_n200 improves accuracy, it opens a promising direction for the remaining 5 experiments (e.g., scvi + multimodal); if not, PCA is confirmed as sufficient and we can pivot to testing multimodal fusion or scgpt. This is the highest-information single-variable test under the limited budget."
